ause of confusion:\r\n\r\n`-a,-b` is going to look for all tests that have neither `a` or `b` tag whereas `a,b` will match all tests that have either `a` or `b` tag. There is no way to select all tests that matches both `a` and `b`.\r\n\r\nThe [documentation](https://docs.bazel.build/versions/master/user-manual.html#flag--test_tag_filters) talks about positive flag as \"required tags\" which leads to believe that we apply a AND whereas it is a OR. The preceding '+' is also confusing... If the '+' sign is not used anywhere, maybe we should make it a way to say always required?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3705/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3705/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":1240641404,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDEyNDA2NDE0MDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/1240641404","actor":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/received_events","type":"User","user_view_t